The above covers this package's own source. It does not cover the artifact it
ships: `php_fmt.phar.br` is PHP CS Fixer's official phar, which bundles the tool
itself, a set of Symfony and ReactPHP components, and their dependencies. All of
it is MIT except `sebastian/diff`, which is BSD-3-Clause.

Every one of those is permissive and asks only for attribution. The notices and
the full texts are in `licenses/NOTICE.md`.

It also does not cover the PHP that runs the fixer. That arrives as an ordinary
npm dependency (`@php-wasm/node-8-4`) rather than being embedded here, so it
carries its own license and is not redistributed by this package.
